WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.922
Think of a family.

2
00:00:01.922 --> 00:00:03.512
If it spends more than it earns

3
00:00:03.512 --> 00:00:04.046
in a year,

4
00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:06.218
it must borrow the difference.

5
00:00:06.218 --> 00:00:07.193
For a government,

6
00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:09.513
that gap is the fiscal deficit.

7
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:11.387
In exam words:

8
00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:14.731
fiscal deficit is total spending minus total

9
00:00:14.731 --> 00:00:17.576
receipts, not counting borrowing.

10
00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:19.166
It is how much the government must

11
00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:20.523
borrow that year.

12
00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:23.477
Say the government spends a hundred and

13
00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:26.542
earns eighty from taxes and other receipts.

14
00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:28.597
It must borrow twenty.

15
00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:31.022
That twenty is the fiscal deficit.

16
00:00:31.421 --> 00:00:33.731
Two cousins: the revenue deficit,

17
00:00:33.731 --> 00:00:36.065
when day-to-day spending exceeds income,

18
00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:37.342
and the primary deficit,

19
00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:39.502
which is the fiscal deficit minus interest

20
00:00:39.502 --> 00:00:40.777
on old loans.

21
00:00:41.177 --> 00:00:42.582
Is a deficit bad?

22
00:00:42.582 --> 00:00:44.730
Borrowing to build roads can pay back.

23
00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.446
But too much borrowing means big interest

24
00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:49.850
bills and less money left for private

25
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.904
business.

26
00:00:51.304 --> 00:00:53.754
The Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management Act

27
00:00:53.754 --> 00:00:56.134
of two thousand three set limits.

28
00:00:56.134 --> 00:00:57.376
In twenty twenty-one,

29
00:00:57.376 --> 00:00:58.897
the government set a path to bring

30
00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:00.546
the deficit below four and a half

31
00:01:00.546 --> 00:01:02.438
percent of GDP by twenty twenty-five,

32
00:01:02.438 --> 00:01:03.678
twenty-six.

33
00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:05.623
For GS Three:

34
00:01:05.623 --> 00:01:08.224
fiscal deficit is the year's borrowing need,

35
00:01:08.224 --> 00:01:10.256
primary deficit leaves out interest,

36
00:01:10.256 --> 00:01:12.924
and the FRBM Act keeps watch.

